# terminal.schema — who may set each key of the `terminal` subsystem (w-conf.md).
# Format: <KEY>\t<scope>   scope: system | user | both
#
# The terminal is a personal choice with a machine-wide default: the admin sets
# what a fresh account gets, each user overrides it with `w-term set <name>`.
TERMINAL	both
# TERMINAL_OPTS is a shell ARRAY, so the layered reader cannot represent it and
# w-term sources that one key itself (see w-conf.md). Declared here for the record.
TERMINAL_OPTS	both
